-- title:
--   Chart prime below a component's generic point is minimal over varpi
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M \neq 0$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $\{p\}$, with $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the image, under the coefficientwise map induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K$, let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra with $\varpi \mapsto 0$. Let $j \in K$ be the element whose Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant, assumed nonzero, and consider the two-chart model over $A$ attached to $(A, K, j)$ with its structure morphism [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252), whose finite chart is the spectrum of the $A$-subalgebra [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgFin`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L135) of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over $A[j]$, immersed by [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.ιFin`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L231). Then for every irreducible component $Z$ of the base change of the model along $\operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, and every point $y$ of the finite chart whose image under the immersion equals the image of the generic point of $Z$ under the first projection, the prime ideal of $y$ is a minimal prime over the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$ in [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgFin`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L135).
--
--   This is the local step identifying the points of the finite chart lying under generic points of the irreducible components of the geometric special fibre as the codimension-one points of that chart modulo the uniformiser, the flatness (going-down) argument that contractions of minimal primes along $A/\varpi \to k$ remain minimal. It is used in the analysis of the components of the special fibre of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$, in particular by the statements describing the images of the two charts and the Gauss-reduction behaviour of the diamond automorphisms on that fibre.
